**GM** — *as Falrinth, warning about his other associates*
> "But there are other friends, and not all of them are as patient as I am."

**GM** — *as Falrinth, warning about Lucius’s return*
> "So, when the flattering man comes again, and he will, do not commit."

**GM** — *as Falrinth*
> "Stall."

**GM** — *as Falrinth, giving a signal*
> "A candle in the West."

**GM** — *as Falrinth, explaining the signal*
> "will reach me. Or don't, report me to Barkinar, he'll believe you. I will simply not be where you tell him I am, but you will have made your choice."

**Zephyr** — *acknowledging*
> "Okay."

**GM** — *as Falrinth, adding one last revelation*
> "And then he says, as he's starting to fade, he says one last thing. One more thing, since you'll hold these wretched halls now. There is a room below, deep, forgotten, on the level beneath your feet."

**GM** — *as Falrinth, revealing the sleeper*
> "The holy gentleman keeps something in it. A sleeper. My leash is short, and the gates are watched. But you, you have keys I never did. If you ever want Verbobonc and all its banners to come down on this terrible… hell… on this temple, and oh, they would come for this, wake what sleeps in the iron coffin."

**GM** — *as Falrinth, giving the final instruction*
> "Ask your golden friend what he's so afraid you'll find, then signal me."

**Zephyr** — *trying to clarify the location*
> "Downstairs, the… Like, the deep purple?"

**GM** — *revealing that the message was one-way*
> "He, he looks at you, and then you realize that this has been a one-way conversation, and he had predicted some of your questions, right?"

**GM** — *describing the illusion’s disappearance*
> "And he… it fades away. So…"

**GM** — *summarizing the uncertainty about the orb*
> "the temple of… the temple… the orb of Golden Death. Either Falrinth has this thing, and he's lying… he's either lying, or he has it."

**GM** — *restating Romag’s account of its power*
> "what you learned from Romag is that it's a very powerful artifact, that if you had it in full possession, you could summon monsters and destroy anything."

**GM** — *summarizing the hidden sleeper*
> "You've also learned that there is something deep forgotten on the level beneath your feet that the Verbobonc would want."
